r><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKEMOTO, HIROFUMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMANAKA, MITSUO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAZAKI, OSAMU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method of reducing an epoxidized organic compound, e.g., a C5-20 (un)saturated epoxy alicyclic organic compound, with hydrogen which comprises contacting the compound with hydrogen in the presence of a nickel catalyst, wherein a basic substance (e.g., an alkali metal hydroxide, alkali metal carbonate, alkali metal alkoxide, or amine having one to three C1-12 alkyl groups) is contained in the reduction system.  Thus, the by-product generation by a deoxidizing side reaction is inhibited and the target compound can be produced in high yield.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé mettant en oeuvre de l'hydrogène pour réduire un composé organique époxydé tel que, par exemple, un composé organique alicyclique époxyde (in)saturé C5-20. Le procédé consiste à placer le composé au contact de l'hydrogène, en présence d'un catalyseur à base de nickel, et à incorporer dans le système de réduction une substance de base (par exemple un hydroxyde métallique alcalin, un carbonate métallique alcalin, un alcoxyde métallique alcalin, ou un amine comprenant un à trois groupes alkyles C1-12). Ce procédé permet d'inhiber une réaction secondaire de désoxydation pouvant générer un sous-produit, et de produire en grande quantité le composé voulu.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>